  "boundary": "Native scalar single-record UPDATE.values assignments without external parameters use the existing exact typed record/tenant permit, captured inputs, prepared seals and final driver carrier. Native mapped keywords and direct-column dictionaries retain types, NULL, native row counts, supported RETURNING, stale identity/refresh, savepoints, failures and current-value removal. Original assignment nodes are validated before and after provider preparation, including async preparation; only an owned statement clone is normalized to sealed external parameters. Original statements remain reusable. The native compiler chooses authenticated RETURNING readers while retaining original ORM projection objects and result-map keys for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE. No new crypto, token, key, index or lifecycle mechanism.",
